window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-234061428b0929bd"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"analyze-product-feedback-across-tools\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">跨工具分析产品反馈</h1> <p>将 Slack 讨论串、问卷导出数据和问题队列整理成清晰的主题与后续事项。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT Work 提供来自 Slack、问卷、问题跟踪工具、客服或研究笔记的反馈。 它可以将反复出现的问题归纳到可供检查的 Sheet 或 Doc 中，包含证据、对设计的 影响、待解决问题和明确的后续事项。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要跨 Slack、问卷、问题单、客服和研究资料检查反馈的团队。</li> <li>需要清晰主题、支持证据和后续事项的产品决策。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取经批准的反馈频道或讨论串链接。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取问题、PR 评论和讨论串。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取缺陷或功能队列。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取反馈文档、导出文件和文件夹，然后创建 Google Doc 或 Sheet。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>分析产品反馈</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">分析关于 [feature or product area] 的反馈，时间范围是 [time period]；使用 @Slack、@GitHub、@Linear 和 @Google Drive。纳入相关的客服工单、问卷和研究笔记。\n\n将反馈归纳为清晰的主题，展示支持证据，并告诉我哪些事项需要关注。\n\n将结果放入 Google Sheet 或 Doc，供我检查。起草后续内容，但不要发布或发送。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾加上 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">开始前</h2> <p>产品反馈可能存在于 Slack、问卷导出数据、问题跟踪工具、客服记录或研究笔记中。向 ChatGPT Work 提供要检查的来源、产品范围和日期区间。它可以将反复出现的问题归纳到一份 Sheet 或 Doc 中，供团队检查，再决定下一步怎么做。</p> <p>在网页版或桌面版 Work 中，使用已连接的应用和云端文件启动这项工作流。如果来源位于你的计算机上，请先附上本地导出文件，或者使用桌面应用。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-expect\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">预期效果</h2> <p>下面是一个关于请求评审队列的示例，使用了问卷导出数据、客服记录、反馈讨论串和研究笔记。第一轮先归纳反复出现的问题；后续再将一个过于宽泛的主题拆分为两个更明确的决策。</p> <p>第一轮从问卷、客服记录、反馈讨论串和研究笔记中发现了三个反复出现的问题：</p> <ul> <li><strong>冲突隐藏在队列中：</strong>四个来源共提及八次。在列表中展示冲突状态，并区分 <code>Ready</code>（就绪）与 <code>Needs attention</code>（需要关注）。</li> <li><strong>批量批准可能包含受阻的请求：</strong>四个来源共提及四次。默认跳过受阻请求，或者在批准前发出警告。</li> <li><strong>评审者会丢失原来的位置，也无法单独筛出要处理的工作：</strong>四个来源共提及十次。保留搜索和筛选状态，并提供 <code>Needs attention</code> 视图。</li> </ul> <p>进一步将最后一个主题拆开后，表格会区分<strong>返回时搜索和筛选状态被重置</strong>，以及<strong>难以单独筛出受阻和未评审的工作</strong>这两个问题。每个主题都保留受影响用户、证据 ID、可信度、对设计的影响、待解决问题和后续事项。这里的数量是小样本中反复提及的次数，不是整个产品的问题发生率。</p> <p><a id=\"how-it-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">运作方式</h2> <ol> <li>向 Work 提供要检查的反馈来源、产品范围和时间区间。</li> <li>请它将重复反馈归纳为主题，并为每个主题保留支持链接或 ID。</li> <li>创建 Google Sheet 或 Doc，包含受影响用户、可信度、待解决问题，以及需要作出的决策或后续事项。</li> <li>在将任何主题整理成 Slack 更新或问题单草稿之前，先检查汇总结果。</li> </ol> <p>第一轮可以使用本页的起步提示词，然后完善那些过于宽泛、缺少证据或混合了不同问题的主题。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-a-reviewed-theme-into-the-next-draft\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">将已检查的主题整理成下一份草稿</h2> <p>有了汇总结果后，可以请 Work 拆分宽泛主题、补充缺失证据、起草 Slack 更新，或者将已检查的主题整理成问题单草稿。指明受众和要作出的决策，让下一步清晰明确。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the feedback summary to draft a short update for [team or channel]. Include the main themes, the evidence, and what we should do next. Don't post it.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">根据反馈摘要，为 [team or channel] 起草一则简短更新。包含主要主题、证据和下一步应该做什么。不要发布。</div></div> <p><a id=\"keep-a-feedback-channel-current\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">持续跟进反馈频道</h2> <p>如果 Slack 频道或问题队列不断收到新的报告，可以请 Work <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-work-from-a-task\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">按计划检查</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。保持相同的检查边界，避免新增反馈变成未经批准的帖子、问题单或任务指派。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check [feedback channel, issue tracker, or survey] every weekday. Tell me when a new theme appears, an existing issue gets worse, or we need to make a decision. Keep the feedback summary up to date, but don't post or send anything.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">每个工作日检查 [feedback channel, issue tracker, or survey]。出现新主题、现有问题恶化，或需要我们作出决定时，告诉我。持续更新反馈摘要，但不要发布或发送任何内容。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"analyze-product-feedback-across-tools\">Analyze product feedback across tools</h1> <p>Turn Slack threads, survey exports, and issue queues into clear themes and follow-ups.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT Work feedback from Slack, surveys, issue trackers, support, or research notes. It can group repeated problems into a reviewable Sheet or Doc with evidence, design implications, open questions, and clear follow-ups.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams reviewing feedback across Slack, surveys, issues, support, and research.</li> <li>Product decisions that need clear themes, supporting evidence, and follow-ups.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved feedback channels or thread links.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github (online)</a></td> <td>Read issues, PR comments, and discussion threads.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear (online)</a></td> <td>Read bug or feature queues.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read feedback docs, exports, and folders, then create a Google Doc or Sheet.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Analyze product feedback</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Analyze feedback on [feature or product area] from [time period] using @Slack, @GitHub, @Linear, and @Google Drive. Include any relevant support tickets, surveys, and research notes.\n\nGroup the feedback into clear themes, show the supporting evidence, and tell me what needs attention.\n\nPut the findings in a Google Sheet or Doc I can review. Draft any follow-ups, but don't post or send them.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Product feedback might live in Slack, survey exports, issue trackers, support records, or research notes. Give ChatGPT Work the sources, product area, and date range to review. It can group repeated problems into a Sheet or Doc the team can check before deciding what to do next.</p> <p>Start this workflow in Work on the web or desktop with connected apps and cloud files. Attach a local export first, or use the desktop app, when the source lives on your computer.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-expect\">What to expect</h2> <p>Here is an example using a survey export, support records, a feedback thread, and research notes for a request-review queue. The first pass groups the repeated problems; the follow-up splits a broad theme into two clearer decisions.</p> <p>The first pass found three repeated problems across a survey, support records, a feedback thread, and research notes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Conflicts are hidden in the queue:</strong> eight mentions across four sources. Show conflict status in the list and distinguish <code>Ready</code> from <code>Needs attention</code>.</li> <li><strong>Bulk approval can include blocked requests:</strong> four mentions across four sources. Skip blocked requests by default or warn before approval.</li> <li><strong>Reviewers lose their place and can't isolate work:</strong> ten mentions across four sources. Preserve search and filters and offer a <code>Needs attention</code> view.</li> </ul> <p>After a follow-up to separate the last theme, the table distinguishes <strong>search and filters resetting on return</strong> from <strong>blocked and unreviewed work being hard to isolate</strong>. The table keeps the affected users, evidence IDs, confidence, design implications, open questions, and follow-ups with each theme. The counts are repeated mentions in a small sample, not product-wide incidence rates.</p> <h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2> <ol> <li>Give Work the feedback sources, product area, and time period to review.</li> <li>Ask it to group repeated feedback into themes and keep supporting links or IDs with each theme.</li> <li>Create a Google Sheet or Doc with affected users, confidence, open questions, and the decision or follow-up needed.</li> <li>Review the summary before turning any theme into a Slack update or issue draft.</li> </ol> <p>Use the starter prompt on this page for the first pass, then refine any theme that is too broad, missing evidence, or mixing separate problems.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-a-reviewed-theme-into-the-next-draft\">Turn a reviewed theme into the next draft</h2> <p>Once the summary exists, ask Work to split a broad theme, add missing evidence, draft a Slack update, or turn a reviewed theme into an issue draft. Name the audience and decision so the next step is clear.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the feedback summary to draft a short update for [team or channel]. Include the main themes, the evidence, and what we should do next. Don't post it.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"keep-a-feedback-channel-current\">Keep a feedback channel current</h2> <p>For a Slack channel or issue queue that keeps getting new reports, ask Work to <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-work-from-a-task\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">check it on a schedule</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>. Keep the same review boundaries so new feedback does not become an unapproved post, issue, or assignment.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check [feedback channel, issue tracker, or survey] every weekday. Tell me when a new theme appears, an existing issue gets worse, or we need to make a decision. Keep the feedback summary up to date, but don't post or send anything.\n</code></pre>"};
